---
import CourseSlideLayout from '../../../../layouts/CourseSlideLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../../../utils/paths';

const title = '2. Research Questions · DEDC02';
const description = 'An interactive lesson on research questions, hypotheses, variables and literature searching.';
const courseHref = withBase('/teaching/courses/dedc02');
const homepageHref = withBase('/');
const comicHref = withBase('/teaching/courses/dedc02/the-claus-hypothesis.png');
---

<CourseSlideLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="pdf-cover" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="eyebrow">DEDC02 · Advanced Research Method</span>
    <h1>Research<br />Questions</h1>
    <div class="pdf-message-block">
      <h2>Personal message</h2>
      <p data-pdf-message-print></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="top-tools" aria-label="Language and timer controls">
    <button class="translate-button global-translate" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-global-translate>中文</button>
    <div class="compact-timer" aria-label="Activity timer">
      <input type="number" min="0.1" step="0.5" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="min" aria-label="Timer minutes" data-timer-minutes />
      <output data-timer-output hidden aria-live="polite">00:00</output>
      <button type="button" data-timer-start>Start</button>
      <button type="button" class="timer-reset-button" data-timer-reset aria-label="Reset timer">↻</button>
      <span class="visually-hidden" data-timer-status role="status" aria-live="assertive"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="deck" aria-label="Research Questions slide deck">
    <section class="slide is-active" data-title="Research Questions" aria-hidden="false">
      <div class="slide-inner title-slide">
        <header class="slide-header title-header">
          <span class="eyebrow">DEDC02 · Advanced Research Method</span>
          <button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button>
        </header>
        <div class="title-rule"></div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h1>Research<br />Questions</h1>
          <p class="lead">How different research paradigms shape research questions for the same topic.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h1>研究<br />問題</h1>
          <p class="lead">不同的研究範式如何塑造同一主題的研究問題。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Learning aims" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Where we are going</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>By the end, you can…</h2>
          <ol class="number-list">
            <li><span><strong>Explain</strong> a research problem.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Distinguish</strong> types of research questions and hypotheses.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Identify and categorise</strong> variables.</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>Search</strong> the literature using keywords.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>完成本課後，你可以⋯⋯</h2>
          <ol class="number-list">
            <li><span><strong>解釋</strong>研究課題。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>區分</strong>研究問題與假設的類型。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>識別並分類</strong>變量。</span></li>
            <li><span><strong>使用關鍵詞</strong>檢索文獻。</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Research questions and paradigm" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research questions and paradigm</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Research questions and paradigm</h2>
          <blockquote>How different research paradigms shape research questions for the same topic:</blockquote>
          <p class="topic-line">“Language learning, achievement and emotions in informal digital learning contexts”</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究問題與研究範式</h2>
          <blockquote>不同的研究範式如何塑造同一主題的研究問題：</blockquote>
          <p class="topic-line">「非正式數字學習環境中的語言學習、成就和情感」</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Three paradigm examples" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research questions and paradigm</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Three paradigms, one topic</h2>
          <div class="paradigm-three">
            <article><h3>Positivism</h3><p class="focus">Measurable, observable, causal relationships</p><p>To what extent do self-reported emotions (e.g., enjoyment, anxiety) predict variance in achievement in informal digital learning contexts?</p></article>
            <article><h3>Constructivism</h3><p class="focus">Learners’ meaning-making, multiple realities</p><p>How do learners construct their understanding of “achievement” when engaging in informal digital language learning?</p></article>
            <article><h3>Pragmatism</h3><p class="focus">Practical outcomes, mixed methods</p><p>Which combination of emotional regulation strategies and digital learning practices most effectively enhance language achievement in informal contexts?</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>三種研究範式，同一主題</h2>
          <div class="paradigm-three">
            <article><h3>實證主義</h3><p class="focus">可測量、可觀察、因果關係</p><p>自我報告的情緒（例如愉悅、焦慮）在多大程度上預測非正式數字學習環境中的成就差異？</p></article>
            <article><h3>建構主義</h3><p class="focus">學習者的意義建構、多重現實</p><p>學習者在進行非正式數字語言學習時，如何建構對「成就」的理解？</p></article>
            <article><h3>實用主義</h3><p class="focus">實際結果、混合方法</p><p>哪種情緒調節策略與數字學習實踐的組合最能有效提升非正式情境中的語言成就？</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Research problem" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research problem</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Research problem</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">To locate the research problem in a study, ask yourself the following:</p>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li>What was the issue, problem or controversy that the researcher wanted to address?</li>
            <li>What controversy leads to a need for this study?</li>
            <li>What was the concern being addressed “behind” this study?</li>
            <li>Is there a sentence like “The problem addressed in this study is…”?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究課題</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">要找出一項研究中的研究課題，請問自己：</p>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li>研究者想要處理的議題、問題或爭議是甚麼？</li>
            <li>甚麼爭議導致需要進行這項研究？</li>
            <li>這項研究「背後」正在處理的關注是甚麼？</li>
            <li>文中是否有一句類似「本研究處理的問題是……」？</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Topics to avoid" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Topics to avoid</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Topics to avoid</h2>
          <div class="avoid-grid">
            <details><summary>Too big</summary><p>Some very large projects can be worthy and valuable to an organisation, but ask whether you have the time, experience and resources to complete them.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Too trivial</summary><p>Ask whether the results have meaning or significance to others, not just to yourself. A project on <em>reducing paper use in a marketing department of ten people</em> may yield little value; studying recycling across an organisation—paper, printer cartridges, furniture and computers—has broader scope.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Lacking in resource materials</summary><p>Look for warning signs: very few references to the topic in the main textbooks, practitioner journals, refereed journals or credible websites.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Lacking in sponsorship</summary><p>Support and commitment from key people in the organisation or fieldwork setting may be important. These may include directors, senior managers, or leaders of networks and groups.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Intractable</summary><p>Be suspicious of a problem that nobody else has been able to solve. Ask yourself: “Why me?” It may be an offer you need to refuse.</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>應避免的主題</h2>
          <div class="avoid-grid">
            <details><summary>範圍太大</summary><p>有些大型項目對組織可能值得且有價值，但要問自己是否有足夠時間、經驗與資源完成它。</p></details>
            <details><summary>過於瑣碎</summary><p>問自己研究結果對其他人是否有意義或重要性，而不只對自己有意義。研究<strong>如何在一個十人的營銷部門減少紙張使用</strong>可能價值很少；研究<strong>整個組織的回收問題（紙張、打印機墨盒、家具、計算機等）</strong>則有更廣泛的範圍。</p></details>
            <details><summary>缺乏資源材料</summary><p>留意警號：主要教科書、實務期刊、同儕評審期刊或可靠網站中，很少提到這個主題或提供相關參考資料。</p></details>
            <details><summary>缺乏贊助</summary><p>研究所在的組織或實地考察環境中，關鍵人士的支持與承諾可能很重要，例如董事、高級管理人員，或網絡與群組的領袖。</p></details>
            <details><summary>棘手的問題</summary><p>對一個其他人都未能解決的問題保持懷疑，並問自己：「為甚麼是我？」這可能是你需要拒絕的提議。</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 1: Narrowing down" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 1: Narrowing down</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Narrowing down</h2>
          <div class="narrowing-activity">
            <ul class="source-list compact-list">
              <li>Technology-Enhanced Language Learning</li>
              <li>Assessment and Feedback in Education</li>
              <li>Motivation, Emotions, and Wellbeing in Learning</li>
              <li>Multilingualism and Identity in Education</li>
              <li>AI Literacy in Digital Education</li>
              <li>Or…</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="intro-line">After background reading and a literature review, use PICO—Population, Intervention, Comparator and Outcome—to keep a research question focused and clinically relevant.</p>
            <div class="pico-guides">
              <article><span class="pico-label">P</span><h3>Population</h3><p>Who is the study relevant to? <strong>Example:</strong> undergraduate students enrolled in digital education courses.</p></article>
              <article><span class="pico-label">I</span><h3>Intervention</h3><p>What exposure, programme or treatment is examined? <strong>Example:</strong> a structured AI-literacy module that teaches students to understand, use, evaluate and ethically apply AI.</p></article>
              <article><span class="pico-label">C</span><h3>Comparator</h3><p>What will it be compared with? <strong>Example:</strong> students receiving usual digital-education support without the module.</p></article>
              <article><span class="pico-label">O</span><h3>Outcome</h3><p>What is expected to change or matter to participants? <strong>Example:</strong> AI-literacy questionnaire scores.</p></article>
            </div>
            <p class="pico-question"><strong>Worked example:</strong> Among undergraduate students enrolled in digital education courses, does a structured AI-literacy module, compared with usual digital-education support without the module, improve AI-literacy questionnaire scores?</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>收窄主題</h2>
          <div class="narrowing-activity">
            <ul class="source-list compact-list">
              <li>科技增強的語言學習</li>
              <li>教育中的評估與回饋</li>
              <li>學習中的動機、情緒與幸福感</li>
              <li>教育中的多語言與身份認同</li>
              <li>數字教育中的人工智能素養</li>
              <li>或者……</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="intro-line">完成背景閱讀與文獻綜述後，可使用 PICO——研究對象（Population）、干預（Intervention）、比較／對照（Comparator／Control）與結果（Outcome）——聚焦研究問題，並保持臨床相關性。</p>
            <div class="pico-guides">
              <article><span class="pico-label">P</span><h3>研究對象</h3><p>研究與誰相關？<strong>例：</strong>修讀數字教育課程的本科生。</p></article>
              <article><span class="pico-label">I</span><h3>干預</h3><p>研究哪一種暴露、方案或治療？<strong>例：</strong>結構化人工智能素養單元，教授學生理解、使用、評估並合乎倫理地應用人工智能。</p></article>
              <article><span class="pico-label">C</span><h3>比較／對照</h3><p>與甚麼比較？<strong>例：</strong>未接受該單元、只接受一般數字教育支援的學生。</p></article>
              <article><span class="pico-label">O</span><h3>結果</h3><p>預期會改變或對參與者重要的是甚麼？<strong>例：</strong>人工智能素養問卷分數。</p></article>
            </div>
            <p class="pico-question"><strong>例子：</strong>在修讀數字教育課程的本科生中，與只接受一般數字教育支援而未接受該單元的學生相比，結構化人工智能素養單元能否提高人工智能素養問卷分數？</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 2: Building up your research" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 2: Building up your research</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Building up your research</h2>
          <div class="build-form" data-build-examples>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="topic-example" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="topic-example">Topic</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-topic">Topic</label>
                <textarea id="build-topic" data-save="topic" placeholder="The broad subject matter addressed by the study."></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="topic-example" hidden><strong>Example:</strong> Distance learning.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="problem-example" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="problem-example">Problem</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-problem">Problem</label>
                <textarea id="build-problem" data-save="problem" placeholder="A general educational issue, concern, or controversy addressed in research that narrows the topic."></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="problem-example" hidden><strong>Example:</strong> Lack of students in distance education classes.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="purpose-example" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="purpose-example">Purpose</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-purpose">Purpose</label>
                <textarea id="build-purpose" data-save="purpose" placeholder="The major intent or objective of the study used to address the problem."></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="purpose-example" hidden><strong>Example:</strong> To study why students do not attend distance education classes at a community college.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="question-example" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="question-example">Question</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-question">Question</label>
                <textarea id="build-question" data-save="question" placeholder="Research questions narrow the purpose into specific questions that the researcher would like answered or addressed in the study."></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="question-example" hidden><strong>Example:</strong> Does the use of Web site technology in the classroom deter students from enrolling in a distance education class?</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>逐步建立你的研究</h2>
          <div class="build-form" data-build-examples>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="topic-example-zh" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="topic-example-zh">主題</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-topic-zh">主題</label>
                <textarea id="build-topic-zh" data-save="topic-zh" placeholder="研究涉及的廣泛主題"></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="topic-example-zh" hidden><strong>例子：</strong>遠距學習。</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="problem-example-zh" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="problem-example-zh">研究課題</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-problem-zh">研究課題</label>
                <textarea id="build-problem-zh" data-save="problem-zh" placeholder="在縮小主題範圍的研究中解決的一般教育問題、關注點或爭議"></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="problem-example-zh" hidden><strong>例子：</strong>遠程教育課程缺乏學生。</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="purpose-example-zh" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="purpose-example-zh">研究目的</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-purpose-zh">研究目的</label>
                <textarea id="build-purpose-zh" data-save="purpose-zh" placeholder="用於解決問題的研究的主要意圖或目標"></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="purpose-example-zh" hidden><strong>例子：</strong>研究為什麼學生不參加社區大學的遠程教育課程。</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="build-field">
              <button type="button" class="build-label" data-build-example-toggle="question-example-zh" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="question-example-zh">研究問題</button>
              <div class="build-entry">
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="build-question-zh">研究問題</label>
                <textarea id="build-question-zh" data-save="question-zh" placeholder="研究問題將目的縮小到研究人員希望在研究中回答或解決的特定問題"></textarea>
                <p class="build-example" id="question-example-zh" hidden><strong>例子：</strong>在課堂上使用網站技術是否會阻止學生參加遠程教育課程？</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Devising research questions" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Devising research questions</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Devising research questions</h2>
          <p class="lead medium">Research questions are not the start of the research; typically they stem from the overall research purposes, objectives and design.</p>
          <p class="intro-line">A useful approach is to ask questions that start with:</p>
          <div class="word-line"><span>what</span><span>what if</span><span>who</span><span>when</span><span>where</span><span>which</span><span>whence</span><span>whither</span><span>why</span><span>how</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>擬定研究問題</h2>
          <p class="lead medium">研究問題不是研究的開始；通常它源於整體研究目的、目標與設計。</p>
          <p class="intro-line">一種有用的方法，是提出以下詞語開頭的問題：</p>
          <div class="word-line"><span>甚麼</span><span>如果</span><span>誰</span><span>何時</span><span>何地</span><span>哪一個</span><span>從何而來</span><span>去往何方</span><span>為甚麼</span><span>如何</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Types of research questions" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Devising research questions</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Types of research questions</h2>
          <div class="type-grid">
            <details><summary>Descriptive</summary><p>What is happening? Describe facts, patterns or situations.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Exploratory</summary><p>What might be going on? Explore under-researched or new areas.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Explanatory</summary><p>Why or how does this happen? Identify causes, mechanisms or relationships.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Comparative</summary><p>How do groups, contexts or interventions differ?</p></details>
            <details><summary>Predictive</summary><p>What will happen? Forecast outcomes based on variables.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Evaluative</summary><p>How effective is this? Assess quality, impact or success.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Development-related</summary><p>How can we create or improve something? Focus on innovation/design.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Normative</summary><p>What should be? Address values, ethics or policy.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Emancipatory</summary><p>How can inequalities be challenged? Give voice to the marginalised.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Empowerment</summary><p>How can people gain agency? Enable learners, teachers or communities to take control.</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究問題的類型</h2>
          <div class="type-grid">
            <details><summary>描述性</summary><p>正在發生甚麼？描述事實、模式或情況。</p></details>
            <details><summary>探索性</summary><p>可能正在發生甚麼？探索研究不足或新的領域。</p></details>
            <details><summary>解釋性</summary><p>為甚麼或如何發生？確定原因、機制或關係。</p></details>
            <details><summary>比較性</summary><p>群體、情境或干預有何不同？</p></details>
            <details><summary>預測性</summary><p>將會發生甚麼？根據變量預測結果。</p></details>
            <details><summary>評估性</summary><p>成效如何？評估品質、影響或成功。</p></details>
            <details><summary>發展相關</summary><p>如何創造或改進某項事物？聚焦創新／設計。</p></details>
            <details><summary>規範性</summary><p>應該怎樣？處理價值、倫理或政策。</p></details>
            <details><summary>解放性</summary><p>如何挑戰不平等？讓邊緣群體發聲。</p></details>
            <details><summary>賦權性</summary><p>人們如何獲得能動性？讓學習者、教師或社群掌握主導權。</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Research questions to avoid" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research questions to avoid</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Research questions to avoid</h2>
          <div class="avoid-question-grid">
            <details><summary>Multiple questions at a time</summary><p>What are the test scores of females and males… and how can we account for such findings?</p></details>
            <details><summary>False dichotomies</summary><p>Is a centralised university entrance examination a narrowing of the curriculum or a fair basis for comparing student performance?</p></details>
            <details><summary>Making false assumptions</summary><p>Why do males prefer multiple-choice questions to essay questions in public English language examinations at age 16?</p></details>
            <details><summary>Tautological questions</summary><p>Why do so many wealthy students study in elite universities?</p></details>
            <details><summary>Too broad</summary><p>What are the effects of such-and-such an intervention on students?</p></details>
            <details><summary>Too simple</summary><p>How are schools addressing student under-achievement?</p></details>
            <details><summary>Biased and leading</summary><p>Avoid “can”/“how can” questions, as these are hypothetical and limitless.</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>應避免的研究問題</h2>
          <div class="avoid-question-grid">
            <details><summary>一次提出多個問題</summary><p>某國 14 歲女性和男性的國際閱讀理解測試成績是多少？我們又如何解釋這些發現？</p></details>
            <details><summary>錯誤的二分法</summary><p>一個國家的集中式大學入學考試是收窄課程，還是公平比較學生成績的依據？</p></details>
            <details><summary>作出錯誤假設</summary><p>為甚麼男性在 16 歲公開英語考試中更喜歡選擇題而不是論述題？</p></details>
            <details><summary>同義反覆問題</summary><p>為甚麼那麼多富裕學生入讀頂尖大學？</p></details>
            <details><summary>範圍過廣</summary><p>某項干預對學生有甚麼影響？</p></details>
            <details><summary>過於簡單</summary><p>學校如何處理學生成績不佳？</p></details>
            <details><summary>有偏見和引導性</summary><p>避免「可以／如何可以」問題，因為這些問題是假設性並且沒有界限。</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="How many research questions?" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">How many research questions should I have?</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>How many research questions should I have?</h2>
          <p class="lead medium">Whilst there are no hard and fast rules, a general principle is to have as few as necessary, but no fewer.</p>
          <p class="intro-line">Research questions may comprise:</p>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li>A question that asks for descriptive data: what, who, where, when</li>
            <li>A question that requires comparisons, differences or relations to be drawn</li>
            <li>A question that asks “so what?”: implications and recommendations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>應該有多少條研究問題？</h2>
          <p class="lead medium">雖然沒有硬性規定，一般原則是盡可能少，但不能更少。</p>
          <p class="intro-line">研究問題可以包括：</p>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li>要求描述性資料的問題：甚麼、誰、何地、何時</li>
            <li>需要比較、差異或關係的問題</li>
            <li>追問「那又怎樣？」的問題：影響與建議</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 3: Revise your research questions" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 3: Building up your research</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Revise your research questions</h2>
          <div class="build-form">
            <label><span>Topic</span><textarea data-save="revise-topic" placeholder="The broad subject matter addressed by the study."></textarea></label>
            <label><span>Problem</span><textarea data-save="revise-problem" placeholder="A general educational issue, concern, or controversy addressed in research that narrows the topic."></textarea></label>
            <label><span>Purpose</span><textarea data-save="revise-purpose" placeholder="The major intent or objective of the study used to address the problem."></textarea></label>
            <label><span>Question</span><textarea data-save="revise-question" placeholder="Research questions narrow the purpose into specific questions that the researcher would like answered or addressed in the study."></textarea></label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>修訂你的研究問題</h2>
          <div class="build-form">
            <label><span>主題</span><textarea data-save="revise-topic-zh" placeholder="研究涉及的廣泛主題"></textarea></label>
            <label><span>研究課題</span><textarea data-save="revise-problem-zh" placeholder="在縮小主題範圍的研究中解決的一般教育問題、關注點或爭議"></textarea></label>
            <label><span>研究目的</span><textarea data-save="revise-purpose-zh" placeholder="用於解決問題的研究的主要意圖或目標"></textarea></label>
            <label><span>研究問題</span><textarea data-save="revise-question-zh" placeholder="研究問題將目的縮小到研究人員希望在研究中回答或解決的特定問題"></textarea></label>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Research questions and hypotheses" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research questions and hypotheses</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Research questions and hypotheses</h2>
          <div class="compare-table">
            <article><h3>Qualitative research</h3><ul><li>Uses research questions</li><li>Seeks information on a single concept</li><li>Asks participants to share ideas and builds general themes</li><li>Uses a more open-ended stance</li><li>Seeks a deep understanding of the views of one group or single individuals</li></ul></article>
            <article><h3>Quantitative research</h3><ul><li>Uses hypotheses</li><li>Identifies and measures multiple variables</li><li>Tests theories that predict results from relating variables</li><li>Uses a closed-ended stance and selects instruments before the study begins</li><li>Measures differences among groups or changes over time</li></ul></article>
          </div>
          <p class="hypothesis-note">Many qualitative studies do not test hypotheses; they explore questions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究問題與假設</h2>
          <div class="compare-table">
            <article><h3>定性研究</h3><ul><li>使用研究問題</li><li>尋求有關單一概念的資料</li><li>請參與者分享想法，並建立一般主題</li><li>採用較開放的立場</li><li>深入理解一個群體或個別人士的觀點</li></ul></article>
            <article><h3>定量研究</h3><ul><li>使用假設</li><li>識別並測量多個變量</li><li>檢驗從變量關係預測結果的理論</li><li>採用封閉式立場，並在研究開始前選擇工具</li><li>測量群體差異或個體隨時間的變化</li></ul></article>
          </div>
          <p class="hypothesis-note">許多定性研究不檢驗假設，而是探索研究問題。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Hypothesis" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Hypothesis</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Hypothesis</h2>
          <div class="hypothesis-introduction">
            <div class="hypothesis-definition">
              <p class="lead medium">A hypothesis is a precise, testable prediction about the relationship between two or more variables. It should be grounded in theory or prior evidence, and the data should be able to show that it is wrong.</p>
              <p class="lead medium">It is not simply an “educated guess”: a research question stays open, while a hypothesis commits to a specific expected pattern.</p>
              <div class="reasoning-compare">
                <aside class="inductive-callout"><strong>Inductive reasoning</strong><span>Moves from observations or patterns to a tentative hypothesis. It helps generate a hypothesis, but does not prove it.</span></aside>
                <aside class="deductive-callout"><strong>Deductive reasoning</strong><span>Starts with a theory or hypothesis and derives a testable prediction. It helps test whether evidence is consistent with the hypothesis.</span></aside>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figure class="comic-figure">
              <img src={comicHref} alt="The Claus Hypothesis comic: observations about Santa lead to the provisional conclusion that Santa Claus is a professor, followed by a null-hypothesis joke." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption>Inductive reasoning in a comic: <a href="https://phdcomics.com/comics/archive_print.php?comicid=1457" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><em>The Claus Hypothesis</em></a> by Jorge Cham.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>假設</h2>
          <div class="hypothesis-introduction">
            <div class="hypothesis-definition">
              <p class="lead medium">假設是對兩個或以上變量之間關係的精確、可檢驗預測。它應以理論或既有證據為基礎，而資料應能顯示它可能是錯的。</p>
              <p class="lead medium">假設不只是「有根據的猜測」：研究問題保持開放，而假設則承諾一種具體的預期模式。</p>
              <div class="reasoning-compare">
                <aside class="inductive-callout"><strong>歸納推理</strong><span>從觀察或模式走向暫時性假設；有助於提出假設，但不能證明假設。</span></aside>
                <aside class="deductive-callout"><strong>演繹推理</strong><span>從理論或假設推導可檢驗的預測；有助於檢驗證據是否與假設一致。</span></aside>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figure class="comic-figure">
              <img src={comicHref} alt="《聖誕老人假設》漫畫：幾項關於聖誕老人的觀察引出聖誕老人是教授的暫時結論，並以零假設作笑點。" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption>漫畫中的歸納推理：Jorge Cham 的<a href="https://phdcomics.com/comics/archive_print.php?comicid=1457" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><em>《The Claus Hypothesis》</em></a>。</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide operationalization-slide" data-title="Operationalization" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From ideas to evidence</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Operationalization</h2>
          <p class="lead small-lead">Operationalization turns an abstract research question or hypothesis into observable participants, conditions, measures and outcomes.</p>
          <div class="operationalization-layout">
            <div class="operationalization-example">
              <div class="operationalization-card question-card"><span class="operationalization-label">Research question</span><p>How do students experience digital feedback on their writing?</p></div>
              <div class="operationalization-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
              <div class="operationalization-details">
                <div><strong>Students</strong><span>second-year undergraduate EFL learners at a university</span></div>
                <div><strong>Experience</strong><span>learners’ perceptions, emotions and interpretations of feedback</span></div>
                <div><strong>Digital feedback</strong><span>teacher comments through an online platform: typed comments and tracked changes</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="operationalization-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
              <div class="operationalization-card refined-card"><span class="operationalization-label">Narrowed qualitative question</span><p>How do second-year undergraduate EFL learners describe their perceptions and experiences of receiving digital feedback (typed comments on drafts) in academic writing courses?</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>操作化</h2>
          <p class="lead small-lead">操作化把抽象的研究問題或假設轉化為可觀察的參與者、條件、測量方式與結果。</p>
          <div class="operationalization-layout">
            <div class="operationalization-example">
              <div class="operationalization-card question-card"><span class="operationalization-label">研究問題</span><p>學生如何體驗寫作中的數字回饋？</p></div>
              <div class="operationalization-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
              <div class="operationalization-details">
                <div><strong>學生</strong><span>大學二年級本科 EFL 學習者</span></div>
                <div><strong>體驗</strong><span>學習者對回饋的看法、情緒與詮釋</span></div>
                <div><strong>數字回饋</strong><span>透過線上平台提供的教師評語：鍵入的評語與修訂記錄</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="operationalization-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
              <div class="operationalization-card refined-card"><span class="operationalization-label">收窄後的定性問題</span><p>大學二年級本科 EFL 學習者如何描述他們在學術寫作課程中接受數字回饋（草稿上的鍵入評語）的看法與經驗？</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Null and alternative hypotheses" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The null and alternative hypotheses</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Null and alternative hypotheses</h2>
          <div class="hypothesis-pair">
            <article><h3>Null hypothesis H₀</h3><p>Tests in the general population that there is no change, no relationship or no difference.</p><p class="formula">There is no difference (or relationship) between…</p></article>
            <article><h3>Alternative hypothesis H₁, H₂, H₃…</h3><p>May be true if the null is rejected; suggests a change, relationship or difference.</p><p class="formula">Higher · lower · more positive · more favourable</p></article>
          </div>
          <h3 class="hypothesis-subtitle">Example</h3>
          <div class="hypothesis-example">
            <article class="hypothesis-example-null"><h3>Null hypothesis (H₀)</h3><p>There is no significant difference in academic-writing scores between students who receive digital feedback and those who receive handwritten feedback.</p></article>
            <article class="hypothesis-example-alternative"><h3>Alternative hypothesis (H₁)</h3><p>Students who receive digital feedback achieve significantly higher academic-writing scores than those who receive handwritten feedback.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>零假設與備擇假設</h2>
          <div class="hypothesis-pair">
            <article><h3>零假設 H₀</h3><p>在一般母體中檢驗沒有變化、沒有關係或沒有差異。</p><p class="formula">……之間沒有差異（或關係）</p></article>
            <article><h3>備擇假設 H₁、H₂、H₃……</h3><p>若零假設被拒絕，則可能成立；表示有變化、關係或差異。</p><p class="formula">較高 · 較低 · 更正面 · 更有利</p></article>
          </div>
          <h3 class="hypothesis-subtitle">例子</h3>
          <div class="hypothesis-example">
            <article class="hypothesis-example-null"><h3>零假設（H₀）</h3><p>接受數字回饋與接受手寫回饋的學生，其學術寫作分數沒有顯著差異。</p></article>
            <article class="hypothesis-example-alternative"><h3>備擇假設（H₁）</h3><p>接受數字回饋的學生，其學術寫作分數顯著高於接受手寫回饋的學生。</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Types of hypotheses" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Choose the claim carefully</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Types of hypotheses</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">First decide whether you are comparing groups or examining an association. Then decide whether prior theory or evidence justifies predicting a direction.</p>
          <div class="hypothesis-type-grid">
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Difference · non-directional</span><h3>Difference without a direction</h3><p>Compares groups but does not say which group will score higher.</p><p class="type-example"><strong>Example:</strong> AI-literacy scores differ between students who receive structured AI-literacy instruction and students who do not.</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Difference · directional</span><h3>Difference with a direction</h3><p>Compares groups and predicts which way the outcome will differ.</p><p class="type-example"><strong>Example:</strong> Students who receive structured AI-literacy instruction will have higher AI-literacy scores than students who do not.</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Correlation · non-directional</span><h3>Association without a direction</h3><p>States that two measured variables are related without predicting a positive or negative pattern.</p><p class="type-example"><strong>Example:</strong> AI-literacy scores are associated with academic-writing scores.</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Correlation · directional</span><h3>Association with a direction</h3><p>States whether the association is positive or negative.</p><p class="type-example"><strong>Example:</strong> Higher AI-literacy scores are positively associated with higher academic-writing scores.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="hypothesis-caution"><strong>Plan before seeing the data:</strong> choose a directional or non-directional form in advance. An association alone does not establish causation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>假設的類型</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">先決定你是在比較群體，還是在檢驗變量之間的關聯；再決定既有理論或證據是否足以支持方向性的預測。</p>
          <div class="hypothesis-type-grid">
            <article><span class="type-kicker">差異 · 非方向性</span><h3>沒有方向的差異</h3><p>比較群體，但不說明哪一個群體的分數較高。</p><p class="type-example"><strong>例子：</strong>接受結構化人工智能素養教學與未接受教學的學生，其人工智能素養分數存在差異。</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">差異 · 方向性</span><h3>有方向的差異</h3><p>比較群體，並預測結果差異的方向。</p><p class="type-example"><strong>例子：</strong>接受結構化人工智能素養教學的學生，其人工智能素養分數將高於未接受教學的學生。</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">相關 · 非方向性</span><h3>沒有方向的關聯</h3><p>指出兩個測量變量有關聯，但不預測正向或負向模式。</p><p class="type-example"><strong>例子：</strong>人工智能素養分數與學術寫作分數相關。</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">相關 · 方向性</span><h3>有方向的關聯</h3><p>指出關聯是正向還是負向。</p><p class="type-example"><strong>例子：</strong>人工智能素養分數越高，通常與越高的學術寫作分數呈正相關。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="hypothesis-caution"><strong>在查看資料前先作規劃：</strong>預先選擇方向性或非方向性的表述。單憑關聯不能確立因果關係。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Hypothesis templates" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From question to prediction</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Hypothesis templates</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">Replace the brackets with your population, variables, measures and comparison. Use a direction only when theory or prior evidence supports it.</p>
          <div class="template-grid">
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Directional difference</span><h3>Compare two groups</h3><p class="template-line">For [population] receiving [condition X], the mean [outcome] score, measured with [instrument], will be [higher/lower] than in [comparison group].</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Directional correlation</span><h3>Relate two variables</h3><p class="template-line">Among [population], [variable A], measured by [instrument], will be [positively/negatively] associated with [variable B], measured by [instrument].</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Moderation</span><h3>Specify a conditional effect</h3><p class="template-line">The relationship between [variable A] and [variable B] in [population] will be [stronger/weaker] at [level of moderator C] than at [comparison level].</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">Null hypothesis</span><h3>State the no-effect claim</h3><p class="template-line">H₀: [outcome] will not differ between [group 1] and [group 2] in [population].</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="hypothesis-caution"><strong>Non-directional option:</strong> say that groups “differ” or variables “are associated” without adding higher, lower, positive or negative.</p>
          <p class="source-note">Template structures adapted from <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI’s hypothesis guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>假設模板</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">把研究對象、變量、測量方式與比較組填入方括號。只有在理論或既有證據支持時，才加入方向。</p>
          <div class="template-grid">
            <article><span class="type-kicker">方向性差異</span><h3>比較兩個群體</h3><p class="template-line">對於接受［條件 X］的［研究對象］，以［工具］測量的平均［結果］分數將［高於／低於］［比較組］。</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">方向性相關</span><h3>連結兩個變量</h3><p class="template-line">在［研究對象］中，以［工具］測量的［變量 A］將與以［工具］測量的［變量 B］呈［正／負］相關。</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">調節作用</span><h3>說明條件性效果</h3><p class="template-line">在［研究對象］中，［變量 A］與［變量 B］的關係，在［調節變量 C 的水平］下將比［比較水平］更［強／弱］。</p></article>
            <article><span class="type-kicker">零假設</span><h3>說明沒有作用的主張</h3><p class="template-line">H₀：在［研究對象］中，［群體 1］與［群體 2］的［結果］沒有差異。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="hypothesis-caution"><strong>非方向性選項：</strong>說明群體「存在差異」或變量「相關」，但不加入較高、較低、正向或負向。</p>
          <p class="source-note">模板結構參考 <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI 假設指引</a>。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Full hypothesis examples" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Specific, testable, grounded</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Full hypothesis examples</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">The weak versions name an idea; the strong versions specify who, what, how it is measured, and—when relevant—when or against whom.</p>
          <div class="full-example-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Example 1 · Difference</h3>
              <div class="weak-strong"><p><span>Weak</span>AI literacy improves writing.</p><p><span>Strong</span>Among first-year undergraduates, students assigned to a four-week AI-literacy workshop will achieve higher mean scores on a common academic-writing rubric than wait-list students at post-test.</p></div>
              <p class="why-example"><strong>Why it works:</strong> It names the population, intervention, comparison, outcome measure and time point; the assigned comparison supports the stated causal design.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Example 2 · Correlation</h3>
              <div class="weak-strong"><p><span>Weak</span>AI literacy is related to achievement.</p><p><span>Strong</span>Among first-year undergraduates, AI-literacy questionnaire scores will be positively associated with academic-writing rubric scores collected in the same semester.</p></div>
              <p class="why-example"><strong>Why it works:</strong> It identifies both measured variables and the direction while avoiding a causal claim.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="source-note">Examples adapted for this course from the strong/weak comparisons in <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI’s hypothesis guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>完整的假設例子</h2>
          <p class="intro-line">較弱的表述只提出一個想法；較強的表述則說明誰、研究甚麼、如何測量，以及在相關情況下何時或與誰比較。</p>
          <div class="full-example-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>例子 1 · 差異</h3>
              <div class="weak-strong"><p><span>較弱</span>人工智能素養改善寫作。</p><p><span>較強</span>在一年級本科生中，被分配參加為期四週人工智能素養工作坊的學生，在共同的學術寫作評分標準上的平均分數，將高於候補名單學生在後測中的分數。</p></div>
              <p class="why-example"><strong>為甚麼可行：</strong>它說明研究對象、干預、比較組、結果測量與時間點；分配式比較配合其因果研究設計。</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>例子 2 · 相關</h3>
              <div class="weak-strong"><p><span>較弱</span>人工智能素養與成就有關。</p><p><span>較強</span>在一年級本科生中，人工智能素養問卷分數將與同一學期收集的學術寫作評分標準分數呈正相關。</p></div>
              <p class="why-example"><strong>為甚麼可行：</strong>它指出兩個可測量變量及關係方向，同時避免提出因果主張。</p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="source-note">例子按本課程需要改編自 <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI 假設指引</a>中的強弱表述比較。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Common hypothesis mistakes" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Quality check</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Common hypothesis mistakes</h2>
          <div class="mistake-grid">
            <article><span>01</span><h3>Too many predictions</h3><p>Split separate outcomes into H₁, H₂ and H₃ so each claim can be tested clearly.</p></article>
            <article><span>02</span><h3>Not falsifiable</h3><p>Name a specific pattern or direction that the data could contradict.</p></article>
            <article><span>03</span><h3>Causal language without a suitable design</h3><p>Use “is associated with” for correlational evidence; reserve causal claims for designs that support them.</p></article>
            <article><span>04</span><h3>No literature grounding</h3><p>Show the logic from theory or prior finding to implication to prediction.</p></article>
            <article><span>05</span><h3>Vague outcome</h3><p>Specify what will change and how it will be measured.</p></article>
            <article><span>06</span><h3>Direction chosen after the data</h3><p>Choose directional or non-directional wording before inspecting the results.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="source-note">Checklist adapted from <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI’s common-mistakes guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>常見的假設錯誤</h2>
          <div class="mistake-grid">
            <article><span>01</span><h3>一個句子有太多預測</h3><p>把不同結果分成 H₁、H₂ 與 H₃，讓每個主張都能清楚檢驗。</p></article>
            <article><span>02</span><h3>無法證偽</h3><p>指出資料可能反駁的具體模式或方向。</p></article>
            <article><span>03</span><h3>研究設計不足卻使用因果語言</h3><p>對相關性證據使用「相關」；只有在研究設計支持時才提出因果主張。</p></article>
            <article><span>04</span><h3>沒有文獻基礎</h3><p>展示由理論或既有發現到推論，再到預測的邏輯。</p></article>
            <article><span>05</span><h3>結果表述含糊</h3><p>說明甚麼會改變，以及如何測量。</p></article>
            <article><span>06</span><h3>看過資料後才選方向</h3><p>在查看結果前，先選擇方向性或非方向性的措辭。</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="source-note">檢查清單參考 <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI 常見錯誤指引</a>。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="How to write a hypothesis" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">A five-step process</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>How to write the hypothesis</h2>
          <ol class="hypothesis-steps">
            <li><span>01</span><strong>Start from the research question</strong><p>Rewrite the question as a statement that commits to a specific answer.</p></li>
            <li><span>02</span><strong>Identify the variables</strong><p>Mark the predictor or Independent Variable (IV) and the outcome or Dependent Variable (DV).</p></li>
            <li><span>03</span><strong>Add measurement detail</strong><p>Name the instrument or operational measure for each variable.</p></li>
            <li><span>04</span><strong>Specify direction if justified</strong><p>Use higher, lower, positive or negative only when theory or evidence supports it.</p></li>
            <li><span>05</span><strong>Pair with a null hypothesis</strong><p>State the no-difference or no-association claim for statistical inference.</p></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="hypothesis-caution"><strong>Before analysis:</strong> record the wording and rationale so the direction is not chosen after seeing the data.</p>
          <p class="source-note">Five-step process adapted from <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI’s hypothesis guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>如何撰寫假設</h2>
          <ol class="hypothesis-steps">
            <li><span>01</span><strong>從研究問題開始</strong><p>把問題改寫成承諾具體答案的陳述。</p></li>
            <li><span>02</span><strong>識別變量</strong><p>標記預測變量或自變量（IV），以及結果或因變量（DV）。</p></li>
            <li><span>03</span><strong>加入測量細節</strong><p>為每一個變量說明工具或操作性測量方式。</p></li>
            <li><span>04</span><strong>在有理據時說明方向</strong><p>只有在理論或證據支持時，才使用較高、較低、正向或負向。</p></li>
            <li><span>05</span><strong>配對零假設</strong><p>為統計推論說明沒有差異或沒有關聯的主張。</p></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="hypothesis-caution"><strong>分析前：</strong>記錄措辭及其理據，避免在查看資料後才選擇方向。</p>
          <p class="source-note">五步流程參考 <a href="https://www.thesisai.io/blog/how-to-write-a-research-hypothesis/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ThesisAI 假設指引</a>。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Concept, construct and variable" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From ideas to measurement</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Concept, construct and variable</h2>
          <div class="concept-grid">
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">01</span><span>Concept</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>A generalisable property or characteristic associated with an object, event or person.</p><p class="example-line">AI literacy is the broad idea of understanding, using and evaluating AI in education.</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">02</span><span>Construct</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>An abstract concept chosen or created to explain a phenomenon. It may combine several related concepts.</p><p class="example-line">AI literacy can be specified as a multidimensional construct involving knowing and understanding AI, using and applying AI, evaluating and corroborating AI-generated content, and incorporating it ethically and effectively (Ng et al., 2024).</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">03</span><span>Variable</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>A measurable representation, or proxy, of a construct. Its value can vary across the cases studied.</p><p class="example-line">An AI literacy questionnaire or scale score is a variable used to represent this construct; its value can differ across learners (Ng et al., 2024; Kim et al., 2026).</p></div></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>概念、構念與變量</h2>
          <div class="concept-grid">
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">01</span><span>概念</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>與物件、事件或人物相關，而且可以概括的屬性或特徵。</p><p class="example-line">人工智能素養是在教育中理解、使用和評估人工智能的廣義概念。</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">02</span><span>構念</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>為解釋某種現象而選擇或創建的抽象概念，可以由幾個相關概念組成。</p><p class="example-line">人工智能素養可以界定為多維構念，包括認識和理解人工智能、使用和應用人工智能、評估和核實人工智能生成的內容，以及以合乎倫理和有效的方式整合這些內容（Ng et al., 2024）。</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">03</span><span>變量</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>構念的可測量表徵或代理指標，其數值可以因研究個案而異。</p><p class="example-line">人工智能素養問卷或量表分數是用來表徵該構念的變量；其數值可以因學習者而異（Ng et al., 2024；Kim et al., 2026）。</p></div></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide concept-measure-slide" data-title="From construct to variable" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From ideas to measurement</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Move from abstract to measurable</h2>
          <div class="illustration-layout">
            <figure>
              <div class="research-plane-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Construct A and Construct B connected by a proposition on the theoretical plane, with corresponding independent and dependent variables connected by a hypothesis on the empirical plane.">
                <div class="diagram-plane theoretical-plane"><span class="plane-label">Theoretical plane</span><span class="diagram-node">Construct A</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>Proposition</small></span><span class="diagram-node">Construct B</span></div>
                <div class="operational-links" aria-hidden="true"><span>↓</span><small>Operationalise</small><span>↓</span></div>
                <div class="diagram-plane empirical-plane"><span class="plane-label">Empirical plane</span><span class="diagram-node">Independent variable</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>Hypothesis</small></span><span class="diagram-node">Dependent variable</span></div>
              </div>
              <figcaption>Constructs become measurable variables through operational definitions.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <ol class="illustration-notes">
              <li><strong>Theoretical plane:</strong> constructs are abstract ideas connected by propositions.</li>
              <li><strong>Operational bridge:</strong> define exactly how each construct will be measured.</li>
              <li><strong>Empirical plane:</strong> variables contain the observed values tested in hypotheses.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="measure-examples">
            <p><strong>Intelligence</strong> <span>construct</span> → <strong>IQ score</strong> <span>variable</span></p>
            <p><strong>Academic achievement</strong> <span>construct</span> → <strong>GPA</strong> <span>variable</span></p>
          </div>
          <p class="measurement-check"><strong>Always ask:</strong> Does this variable represent the construct well?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>從抽象概念走向測量</h2>
          <div class="illustration-layout">
            <figure>
              <div class="research-plane-diagram" role="img" aria-label="理論層面的構念 A 與構念 B 由命題連接，並透過自變量與因變量在經驗層面形成可檢驗的假設。">
                <div class="diagram-plane theoretical-plane"><span class="plane-label">理論層面</span><span class="diagram-node">構念 A</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>命題</small></span><span class="diagram-node">構念 B</span></div>
                <div class="operational-links" aria-hidden="true"><span>↓</span><small>操作化</small><span>↓</span></div>
                <div class="diagram-plane empirical-plane"><span class="plane-label">經驗層面</span><span class="diagram-node">自變量</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>假設</small></span><span class="diagram-node">因變量</span></div>
              </div>
              <figcaption>透過操作性定義，把構念轉化為可測量的變量。</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <ol class="illustration-notes">
              <li><strong>理論層面：</strong>構念是抽象想法，彼此由命題連接。</li>
              <li><strong>操作化橋樑：</strong>明確界定每個構念將如何測量。</li>
              <li><strong>經驗層面：</strong>變量包含觀察所得的數值，並用於檢驗假設。</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="measure-examples">
            <p><strong>智力</strong> <span>構念</span> → <strong>智商分數</strong> <span>變量</span></p>
            <p><strong>學業成就</strong> <span>構念</span> → <strong>平均績點</strong> <span>變量</span></p>
          </div>
          <p class="measurement-check"><strong>始終要問：</strong>這個變量是否能良好地代表該構念？</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 4: The family of variables" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 4: The family of variables</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>The family of variables</h2>
          <div class="variable-form">
            <label>What outcomes in my study am I trying to explain?<textarea data-save="outcomes"></textarea></label>
            <label>What variables or factors influence the outcomes?<textarea data-save="factors"></textarea></label>
            <label>What variables do I need to also measure (i.e., control) so that I can make sure that my major factors influence outcomes and not other factors?<textarea data-save="controls"></textarea></label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>變量家族</h2>
          <div class="variable-form">
            <label>我的研究試圖解釋哪些結果？<textarea data-save="outcomes-zh"></textarea></label>
            <label>哪些變量或因素影響這些結果？<textarea data-save="factors-zh"></textarea></label>
            <label>我還需要測量哪些變量（即控制變量），以確保主要因素而不是其他因素影響結果？<textarea data-save="controls-zh"></textarea></label>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Types of variables" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The family of variables</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Types of variables</h2>
          <div class="variable-types">
            <details><summary>Control variable</summary><p>An extraneous factor whose influence is controlled or held constant. In this example, record relevant background factors so they do not obscure the main relationship.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Independent variable</summary><p>The predictor or proposed cause. Here, <strong>intelligence</strong> is used to predict academic achievement and, through it, earning potential.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Dependent variable</summary><p>The outcome being explained. Here, <strong>earning potential</strong> is the outcome at the end of the model.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Intervening or mediating variable</summary><p>The mechanism between a predictor and an outcome. Here, <strong>academic achievement</strong> carries part of the relationship between intelligence and earning potential.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Moderating variable</summary><p>A factor that changes the strength or direction of a relationship. Here, <strong>effort</strong> moderates the relationship between intelligence and academic achievement.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Covariate</summary><p>A measured variable included to account for variation in the dependent variable. Here, <strong>work experience</strong> is included alongside the main model.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Confounding or lurking variable</summary><p>A rival explanation for the relationship. Here, <strong>socioeconomic background</strong> may influence both intelligence opportunities and earning potential.</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>變量的類型</h2>
          <div class="variable-types">
            <details><summary>控制變量</summary><p>其影響受到控制或保持不變的外來因素。在這個例子中，記錄相關背景因素，避免它們遮蔽主要關係。</p></details>
            <details><summary>自變量</summary><p>預測變量或假定的原因。在這個例子中，<strong>智力</strong>用來預測學業成就，並透過學業成就預測賺取收入的潛力。</p></details>
            <details><summary>因變量</summary><p>被解釋的結果。在這個例子中，<strong>賺取收入的潛力</strong>是模型末端的結果。</p></details>
            <details><summary>介入或中介變量</summary><p>位於預測變量與結果之間的機制。在這個例子中，<strong>學業成就</strong>承載智力與賺取收入的潛力之間的部分關係。</p></details>
            <details><summary>調節變量</summary><p>改變關係強度或方向的因素。在這個例子中，<strong>努力</strong>調節智力與學業成就之間的關係。</p></details>
            <details><summary>協變量</summary><p>納入測量以解釋因變量變異的變量。在這個例子中，<strong>工作經驗</strong>與主要模型一同納入。</p></details>
            <details><summary>混淆或潛伏變量</summary><p>對關係的競爭解釋。在這個例子中，<strong>社會經濟背景</strong>可能同時影響智力發展機會與賺取收入的潛力。</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

